en burying"},{"surface":"உய்ந்தனர்","parts":[{"text":"உய்ந்தனர்","lemma":"உய்","gloss":"escaped"}],"gloss":"they escaped"},{"surface":"மாதோ","parts":[{"text":"மாதோ","lemma":"மாதோ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வரிஞிமிறு","parts":[{"text":"வரி","lemma":"வரி","gloss":"stripe"},{"text":"ஞிமிறு","lemma":"ஞிமிறு","gloss":"bee"}],"gloss":"striped bee"},{"surface":"ஆர்க்கும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்க்கும்","lemma":"ஆர்","gloss":"buzzing"}],"gloss":"buzzing"},{"surface":"வாய்புகு","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"வாய்","gloss":"mouth"},{"text":"புகு","lemma":"புகு","gloss":"entering"}],"gloss":"entering the mouth"},{"surface":"கடாஅத்து","parts":[{"text":"கடாஅத்து","lemma":"கடாம்","gloss":"musth"}],"gloss":"musth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அண்ணல்","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணல்","lemma":"அண்ணல்","gloss":"majestic"}],"gloss":"majestic"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"அடுகளத்","parts":[{"text":"அடுகளத்","lemma":"அடுகளத்","gloss":"on the battlefield"}],"gloss":"on the battlefield","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தொழிய","parts":[{"text":"தொழிய","lemma":"தொழிய","gloss":"to perish"}],"gloss":"to perish","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அருஞ்சமம்","parts":[{"text":"அருமை","lemma":"அருமை","gloss":"difficult"},{"text":"சமம்","lemma":"சமம்","gloss":"battle"}],"gloss":"difficult battle"},{"surface":"ததைய","parts":[{"text":"ததைய","lemma":"ததை","gloss":"shatter"}],"gloss":"to shatter"},{"surface":"நூறி","parts":[{"text":"நூறி","lemma":"நூறு","gloss":"destroy"}],"gloss":"having destroyed"},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருந்","parts":[{"text":"பெருந்","lemma":"பெருந்","gloss":"great"}],"gloss":"great","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தகை","parts":[{"text":"தகை","lemma":"தகை","gloss":"nobility"}],"gloss":"nobility"},{"surface":"விழுப்புண்","parts":[{"text":"விழு","lemma":"விழு","gloss":"glorious"},{"text":"புண்","lemma":"புண்","gloss":"wound"}],"gloss":"glorious wound"},{"surface":"பட்ட","parts":[{"text":"பட்ட","lemma":"படு","gloss":"received"}],"gloss":"received"},{"surface":"மாறே","parts":[{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"மாறு","gloss":"because"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"because"}]}],"literal":"When the firm-bound drum thunders with a roaring sound, / going and conquering in battle is how possible? Those who came, / even withstanding your vanguard they are not able to, and being frightened, / running away is accustomed to those kings without pride. / Due to disease, their perished bodies are embraced, / their loved ones forgetting their affection, in order to remove their sins, / the priests of the four Vedas who practice virtue, / performing the rites, spread green grass and lay them down, / with valor as their support, who fell in good battle, / 'let them go to the place where the warriors wearing long hero's anklets go,' saying, / cleaving with a sword and burying, they indeed escaped! / With musth entered by buzzing striped bees, / leaving the majestic elephants dead on the battlefield, / you, having destroyed and shattered the difficult battle, / because you received a glorious wound of great nobility.","translation":"When your firm-bound war drum thunders with a roaring sound, how can the enemies who come against you ever hope to conquer? Those pride-less kings, accustomed only to fleeing in terror, cannot even withstand your vanguard. Yet, because you shattered the enemy in a fierce battle, leaving their majestic elephants—whose musth-dripping mouths attract buzzing striped bees—dead on the battlefield, and received a glorious wound on your chest, those very kings have escaped a shameful fate! Normally, when such men die of disease, their grieving kin embrace their lifeless bodies, and to cleanse them of the sin of not dying in battle, virtuous priests of the four Vedas spread sacred green grass, lay them down, and cleave their bodies with a sword, saying, 'Let them go to the heaven of brave warriors who fell in battle.' By facing you and dying on the battlefield, those cowardly kings have escaped this post-mortem ritual of being sliced with a sword!","modern":"உன்னுடைய வலிமையான வாரினால் கட்டப்பட்ட முரசு 'இழுமென' என்று முழங்கும்போது, உன்னை எதிர்த்து வந்து போரில் வெல்வது எப்படி இயலும்? உன்னை எதிர்த்து வந்த பகைவர்கள், உனது படைமுகப்பைத் தாங்குவதற்கும் ஆற்றல் இல்லாதவர்கள்; அச்சமுற்று ஓடுவதையே வழக்கமாகக் கொண்ட பெருமையற்ற அரசர்கள் அவர்கள். நோயினால் இறந்துபோன உடலைத் தழுவிக்கொண்டு, சுற்றத்தினர் தம் அன்பை மறந்து, அவர்தம் பாவங்களை நீக்குவதற்காக, அறம் செய்யும் கொள்கையுடைய நான்கு வேதங்களை உணர்ந்த அந்தணர்கள், தர்பைப் புல்லைப் பரப்பி அதன்மேல் உடலைக் கிடத்தி, 'வீரத்தையே பற்றுகோடாகக் கொண்டு நல்ல போரில் வீழ்ந்த, நீண்ட வீரக்கழல் அணிந்த வீரர்கள் செல்லும் வீரசுவர்க்கத்திற்கு இவனும் செல்க' என்று கூறி, உடலை வாளால் பிளந்து அடக்கம் செய்யும் சடங்கிலிருந்து அவர்கள் தப்பித்துக் கொண்டனர்! வண்டுகள் மொய்க்கும் மதநீர் வழியும் வாயையுடைய கம்பீரமான யானைகள் போர்க்களத்தில் மடியுமாறு, அரிய போரைச் சிதைத்து அழித்து, பெருந்தகையாகிய நீ மார்பில் விழுப்புண் பட்டாய் அல்லவா! அதனால், உன்னோடு போரிட்டு மடிந்த பகைவேந்தர்கள் வாளால் பிளக்கப்படும் சடங்கு இல்லாமலேயே வீரசுவர்க்கம் அடைந்தனர்.","explanation":"This poem is addressed to the chieftain Adhiyaman Neduman Anji by the famous poet Avvaiyar, belonging to the Vagai tinai (victory). The poet praises Adhiyaman's extraordinary valor and his noble nature. She describes a unique ancient Tamil custom: when a king or warrior died of disease instead of on the battlefield, it was considered a disgrace. To cleanse this sin and ensure they reached the warriors' heaven, priests would lay the body on sacred grass and symbolically cleave it with a sword before burial. Avvaiyar wittily remarks that Adhiyaman's cowardly enemies, who usually ran away in fear, were saved from this post-mortem mutilation because they died fighting him in actual battle. By giving them a hero's death on the battlefield, Adhiyaman's fierce valor ironically bestowed honor upon his enemies.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.4],[0.4,0.5],[0.5,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.9],[1.9,2.9],[2.9,3.4],[3.4,3.7],[3.7,3.9],[3.9,4.7],[4.7,5.17],[5.17,6.0],[6.0,6.6],[6.6,7.1],[7.1,7.7],[7.7,7.8],[7.8,8.4],[8.4,8.8],[8.8,9.67],[9.67,9.83],[9.83,10.23],[10.23,10.46],[10.8,12.0],[12.0,12.3],[12.3,12.4],[12.4,13.1],[13.1,13.5],[13.5,14.4],[14.4,14.6],[14.6,14.9],[14.9,15.5],[15.5,16.7],[16.7,17.3],[17.3,17.6],[17.6,17.8],[18.84,19.34],[19.34,19.74],[19.74,19.74],[19.74,20.14],[20.14,20.74],[20.74,21.54],[21.54,21.84],[21.84,22.14],[22.14,22.34],[22.34,22.94],[22.94,23.34],[23.34,24.74],[24.79,25.14],[25.14,25.44],[25.44,25.74],[25.74,25.74],[25.74,27.54],[27.54,27.74],[27.74,28.14],[28.14,28.94],[28.94,29.04],[29.04,29.77],[29.77,30.14],[30.14,31.04],[31.04,31.24],[31.24,31.94],[31.94,32.04],[32.04,32.84],[32.84,33.24],[33.24,33.84],[33.84,34.14],[34.14,34.24]],"female":[[0.0,0.4],[0.4,0.7],[0.7,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,2.1],[2.1,3.1],[3.1,3.5],[3.5,3.8],[3.8,4.0],[4.0,4.8],[4.8,5.55],[5.55,6.3],[6.3,6.8],[6.8,7.3],[7.3,8.1],[8.1,8.2],[8.2,9.0],[9.0,9.4],[9.4,10.5],[10.5,10.9],[10.9,11.02],[11.02,11.6],[11.6,12.7],[12.7,13.2],[13.2,13.4],[13.4,14.2],[14.2,14.7],[14.7,15.6],[15.6,15.7],[15.7,16.1],[16.1,16.8],[16.8,18.1],[18.1,18.7],[18.7,19.1],[19.1,19.3],[20.4,21.0],[21.0,21.3],[21.3,21.4],[21.4,21.8],[21.8,22.4],[22.4,23.1],[23.1,23.5],[23.5,23.7],[23.7,24.0],[24.0,24.6],[24.6,25.0],[25.0,26.3],[26.3,26.54],[26.67,27.4],[27.4,27.8],[27.8,27.8],[27.8,29.5],[29.5,29.9],[29.9,30.1],[30.1,31.5],[31.5,31.6],[31.6,32.33],[32.33,32.8],[32.8,33.8],[33.8,34.1],[34.1,34.7],[34.7,34.8],[34.8,35.53],[35.53,35.9],[35.9,36.5],[36.5,36.8],[36.8,36.8]]},"sync":[[["திண்","firm"]],[["பிணி","bound"]],[["முரசம்","drum"]],[["இழுமென","with a roaring sound"]],[["முழங்கச்","to sound"]],[["சென்று","having gone"]],[["அமர்","battle"]],[["கடத்தல்","conquering"]],[["யாவது","how is it possible"]],[["வந்தோர்","those who